{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777130891,"nonce":"HQaYbClkeFd5Xtz9aHlXlw0JGNE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAf_zFA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/87","origin":"github"},"title":"Audit and prune mavros plugin load — switch to explicit allowlist (~80% reduction, 56 → 12 plugins)","message":"## Context\n\nmavros on the BizzyBoat currently uses the **default `apm_pluginlists.yaml`**, which only `denylist`s 8 plugins. That leaves **56 plugins loaded** (verified from the `2026-04-24T17.39.30` session bag's `/rosout` startup window). Only **9 mavros topics** were actively recorded during a 36-minute autonomy-window bag, traceable to **~7 plugins** producing real data, plus a small handful providing services or non-recorded outputs. The remaining ~44 plugins are dead weight: aircraft-only features, vision/mocap feedback we don't run, ESC telemetry our hardware doesn't expose, sim/test fixtures, mission features we deliberately don't use, etc.\n\nThis audit replaces the default `denylist` with an explicit **`allowlist`** sized to what we actually use — ~80% reduction in loaded plugins, no functionality loss.\n\nThe audit was prompted by the 2026-04-24 pier-session investigation into \"FCU mission rejected — nav stack unhealthy\" (see [PR #83 cross-reference comment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/83#issuecomment-4319569786)). The 101× `guided_target: PositionTargetGlobal failed because no origin` warnings during the bag turned out to be noise on a plugin path nothing in our stack uses — but they prompted the question of which plugins are pulling weight at all.\n\n## Proposed allowlist (12 plugins)\n\nReplace the `plugin_denylist` in `apm_pluginlists.yaml` with a `plugin_allowlist` of exactly these:\n\n| Plugin | Justification |\n|---|---|\n| `sys_status` | `/state`, `/battery` — vital FCU heartbeat (recorded in bag) |\n| `global_position` | `/global_position/raw/fix`, `/raw/gps_vel` (recorded; 22k msgs/session) |\n| `gps_status` | `/gpsstatus/gps1/raw` (recorded; 22k msgs/session) |\n| `gps_rtk` | `/gps_rtk/send_rtcm` (recorded; NTRIP RTCM injection) |\n| `imu` | `/imu/data` (recorded; 22k msgs/session) |\n| `rc_io` | `/rc/out` (recorded for diagnostics — see logger config in `bizzyboat.yaml`); reserved for future `/rc/in` recording (see below) and any future winch work via `/rc/override` |\n| `setpoint_velocity` | `/setpoint_velocity/cmd_vel` — the actually-used cmd_vel path to FCU (recorded; 9.7k msgs/session) |\n| `command` | Service path for arm/disarm/set_mode (saw `mavros.cmd: CMD: Unexpected command 520` in /rosout) |\n| `param` | FCU parameter R/W at startup (saw `PR: Param STAT_FLTTIME` in /rosout) |\n| `sys_time` | FCU↔companion clock sync — keep on principle; loss could break sensor-fusion timestamping |\n| `nav_controller_output` | Intentionally recorded for diagnostics (see `bizzyboat.yaml` line 222 logger entry, comment: \"how hard its internal nav controller is working to follow cmd_vel\") |\n| `manual_control` | **Reserved for planned winch control** (see workspace memory `project_winch_via_mavros_manual_control.md`) — currently zero workspace consumers, but kept loaded so the future host-side winch publisher to `/mavros/manual_control/send` doesn't require a plugin re-enable |\n\n## Plugins to drop (44)\n\nGrouped by reason:\n\n- **Aircraft-only**: `adsb`, `vfr_hud`, `wind_estimation`, `terrain` (ArduRover doesn't estimate wind from airspeed/lean — plugin would be silent even if kept)\n- **Vision / mocap feedback (no sensors of these classes in our stack)**: `vision_pose`, `vision_speed`, `optical_flow`, `mocap_pose_estimate`\n- **FCU-managed camera / gimbal hardware (we have ROS-side cameras only)**: `gimbal_control`, `mount_control`, `camera`, `cam_imu_sync`\n- **Aerial / UAV features**: `landing_target`, `open_drone_id`, `obstacle_distance`, `obstacle_distance_3d`\n- **Companion / status reporters with no consumer**: `cellular_status`, `tdr_radio`, `tunnel`, `companion_process_status`, `onboard_computer_status` (see \"Worth revisiting\" below for `companion_process_status`)\n- **Sim / test fixtures**: `sim_state`, `fake_gps`, `gps_input`\n- **ArduPilot mission features (autonomy is cmd_vel-only by design — see workspace memory `project_bizzyboat_autonomy_stack.md`)**: `waypoint`, `rallypoint`, `trajectory`\n- **ESC telemetry (Torqeedo Power 24-3500 over Cube doesn't expose this — see `project_bizzyboat_fcu_params_pending.md`)**: `esc_status`, `esc_telemetry`\n- **Diagnostic / one-shot, easy to re-enable on demand**: `mag_calibration_status`, `log_transfer`, `play_tune`\n- **Sensor not present**: `distance_sensor`, `rangefinder`\n- **Verified zero workspace usage (grepped this session)**: `home_position`, `local_position`, `odometry`\n- **Unused setpoint flavors (only `setpoint_velocity` used)**: `setpoint_accel`, `setpoint_attitude`, `setpoint_position`, `setpoint_raw`, `setpoint_trajectory`\n- **Noise source on a path nothing uses**: `guided_target` (the 101× \"no origin\" warning per session)\n- **Discussed and dropped**: `geofence` (potential future safety feature; one-line re-enable when added)\n\n## Logger config bonus — record `/bizzy/mavros/rc/in`\n\nWhile in `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`, add `/bizzy/mavros/rc/in` to the logger topics next to the existing `/bizzy/mavros/rc/out` entry. This costs ~2 KB/s but gains:\n\n- Operator-action audit trail (which RC channel triggered the GUIDED→MANUAL transition?)\n- Winch knob history (currently the winch is on an RC knob — every adjustment would be logged)\n- Radio-link health post-session\n- Kill-switch / safety-channel evidence\n\nSame plugin (`rc_io`), no plugin-list change needed — just one line in the logger topics list.\n\n## Worth revisiting later (drop now, but flagged)\n\n| Plugin | Re-enable trigger |\n|---|---|\n| `companion_process_status` | If/when we add a companion-heartbeat-emitter so the FCU can drop GUIDED when gabby's nav stack is unhealthy. Real safety win for autonomous survey work; needs publisher node first. |\n| `geofence` | If/when we add survey-polygon enforcement (autonomous survey scope). |\n| `setpoint_raw` | If we ever want to bypass GUIDED-mode global packaging via `FRAME_BODY_NED` (the alternate path mentioned in earlier nav-stack-unhealthy investigation). |\n| `mavros odometry` plugin | Open design question: do we want the FCU's EKF estimate as a parallel/redundant source alongside `mru_transform`? Different fusion (Kalman over GPS+IMU+heading vs. TF-based velocity). Not part of this audit. |\n\n## Open design question (do not block on)\n\nmavros' `odometry` plugin would expose the FCU's EKF estimate as a parallel odometry source. Currently `mru_transform` is the canonical `/bizzy/odom` publisher (different fusion: TF-based velocity vs. Kalman-fused GPS+IMU+heading). Whether to consume both is a design call worth discussing separately.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe `mavros_node` Node action in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/core_launch.py` currently loads three parameter files in order: `apm_pluginlists.yaml` (mavros default) → `apm_config.yaml` (mavros default) → `bizzyboat_project11/config/mavros.yaml` (frame-id overrides). The cleanest place for the allowlist is a new `bizzyboat_project11/config/mavros_pluginlists.yaml` loaded **after** the mavros default — last write wins. Format:\n\n```yaml\n/**:\n  ros__parameters:\n    plugin_allowlist:\n      - sys_status\n      - global_position\n      - gps_status\n      - gps_rtk\n      - imu\n      - rc_io\n      - setpoint_velocity\n      - command\n      - param\n      - sys_time\n      - nav_controller_output\n      - manual_control\n```\n\nWhen `plugin_allowlist` is set, mavros ignores `plugin_denylist` and loads only the allowlist. No need to touch the upstream `apm_pluginlists.yaml`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Bench: bring up the stack on gabby with the new allowlist; confirm mavros logs **only** the 12 plugins loaded, no unexpected \"ignored\" surprises.\n- [ ] Confirm no errors in `/rosout` from the dropped plugins (e.g., no node-init failures).\n- [ ] Verify recorded mavros topics in a short bench bag match expectations: `/state`, `/battery`, `/global_position/raw/fix`, `/raw/gps_vel`, `/gpsstatus/gps1/raw`, `/gps_rtk/send_rtcm`, `/imu/data`, `/rc/in` (new), `/rc/out`, `/setpoint_velocity/cmd_vel`, `/nav_controller_output`.\n- [ ] Confirm autonomy stack still functions: cmd_vel path (joy + autonomous), arm/disarm command service, RC manual override path, RTK injection.\n- [ ] Confirm absence of the 101× `guided_target: PositionTargetGlobal failed because no origin` warning per session.\n- [ ] At next pier session: full system smoke test, mode transitions, manual+autonomous control.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- ~80% reduction in mavros plugin load on gabby — modest CPU/RAM relief.\n- Eliminates `guided_target` warning spam (cleaner /rosout, easier diagnosis of real warnings).\n- Makes the actual mavros surface area auditable in one yaml file.\n- New logger entry adds operator-action / radio-link / winch-knob forensics to every recorded session.\n- Risk: if a future feature needs a dropped plugin, re-enable is one yaml line. The \"Worth revisiting later\" section captures the most likely candidates.\n\n## References\n\n- Bag evidence: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-24T17.39.30.474679495` (loaded-plugin enumeration, mavros topic list, /rosout startup window)\n- Workspace memories: `project_bizzyboat_autonomy_stack.md`, `project_bizzyboat_fcu_params_pending.md`, `project_winch_via_mavros_manual_control.md`\n- Source files: `bizzyboat_project11/launch/core_launch.py` (mavros_node parameters), `bizzyboat_project11/config/mavros.yaml` (frame-id overrides), `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml` (logger config)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}